A loaded die, with faces numbered from $1$ to $6$, has the property that each even face comes up with twice the probability of each odd face. Compute the probabilities of obtaining, in a single throw of the die, respectively:
- a prime number;
- a number at least equal to $3$;
- a number at most equal to $3$.

In space with an orthogonal Cartesian coordinate system $Oxyz$, the plane $\pi: 3x-2y+5=0$ is given.
- Determine the coordinates of the point $H$, the orthogonal projection of $P(4, 2, 1)$ onto the plane $\pi$;
- Determine the intersection of the line $s:\ \begin{cases}x-y+1=0\\ z-2=0\end{cases}$ with the plane $\pi$.

Determine the polynomial function of degree four $y=p(x)$ knowing that, in a Cartesian coordinate system, its graph satisfies the following conditions:
- it is tangent to the $x$-axis at the origin;
- it passes through the point $(1,0)$;
- it has a stationary point at $(2, -2)$.
